 "markdown_file": "Europe/England/075 - News!.md",
 "stats": {
  "paragraphs": 31,
  "segments": 50,
  "words": 289
 },
 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p001.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. Ha!"
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s02",
     "source": "Steward, how are you, my old boy?"
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s03",
     "source": "How do things go on at home?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p001"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p002.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s02",
     "source": "Bad enough, your honour; the magpie's dead!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p002"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p003.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. Poor mag! so he's gone."
    },
    {
     "id": "p003.s02",
     "source": "How came he to die?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p003"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p004.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s02",
     "source": "Over-ate himself, Sir."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p004"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p005.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. Did he indeed? a greedy dog."
    },
    {
     "id": "p005.s02",
     "source": "Why, what did he get that he liked so well?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p005"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p006.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p006.s02",
     "source": "Horseflesh; he died of eating horseflesh."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p006"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p007.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. How came he to get so much horseflesh?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p007"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p008.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p008.s02",
     "source": "All your father's horses, Sir."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p008"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p009.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. What! are they dead too?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p009"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p010.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p010.s02",
     "source": "Ay, Sir; they died of over-work."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p010"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p011.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. And why were they over-worked?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p011"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p012.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p012.s02",
     "source": "To carry water, Sir."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p012"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p013.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. To carry water, and what were they carrying water for?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p013"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p014.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p014.s02",
     "source": "Sure, Sir, to put out the fire."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p014"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p015.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. Fire! what fire?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p015"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p016.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s02",
     "source": "Your father's house is burned down to the ground."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p016"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p017.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. My father's house burnt down! and how came it to be on fire?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p017"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p018.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p018.s02",
     "source": "I think, Sir, it must have been the torches."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p018"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p019.s01",
     "source": "MR G. Torches! what torches?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p019"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p020.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p020.s02",
     "source": "At your mother's funeral."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p020"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p021.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. My mother dead?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p021"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p022.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p022.s02",
     "source": "Ay, poor lady, she never looked up after it."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p022"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p023.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. After what?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p023"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p024.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p024.s02",
     "source": "The loss of your father."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p024"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p025.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. My father gone too?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p025"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p026.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p026.s02",
     "source": "Yes, poor gentleman, he took to his bed as soon as he heard of it."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p026"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p027.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. Heard of what?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p027"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p028.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p028.s02",
     "source": "The bad news, an' it please your honour."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p028"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p029.s01",
     "source": "MR. G. What? more miseries, more bad news!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p029"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p030.s01",
     "source": "STEWARD."
    },
    {
     "id": "p030.s02",
     "source": "Yes, Sir, your bank has failed, your credit is lost and you're not worth a shilling in the world."
    },
    {
     "id": "p030.s03",
     "source": "I make bold, Sir, to come and wait on you about it; for I thought you would like to hear the news."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p030"
  },
  {
   "type": "break",
   "segments": [],
   "id": "p031"
  }
 ]
}